<title>UK: Aluminium stocks fell in February - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium stocks fell in February - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total stocks of all forms of aluminium at Western world smelters excluding finished end-products, fell to 3.077 million tonnes at the end of February 1997, compared with 3.149 million in January and 3.631 million in February 1996, provisional International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) figures show.</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks fell to 1.552 million tonnes versus 1.662 million and 2.025 million, respectively.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of the total aluminium stocks was as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    Feb'97    Jan'97    Feb'96</p>
<p>    Africa		    65	 70	  87</p>
<p>    North America	1,466    1,461     1,721</p>
<p>    Latin America	  137	163	 191</p>
<p>    Asia		     178	183	 173</p>
<p>    Europe		 1,110    1,139     1,311</p>
<p>    Oceania		  121	133	 148</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks were distributed as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			   Feb'97    Jan'97    Feb'96</p>
<p>    Africa		    17	 22	  35</p>
<p>    North America	  635	644	 838</p>
<p>    Latin America	   88	117	 147</p>
<p>    Asia		     137	142	 151</p>
<p>    Europe		   593	643	 745</p>
<p>    Oceania		   82	 94	 109</p>
</text>
